---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="JopChi — Daily Dual-Word Puzzle for iOS">
  <!-- ============================================================
       Hero
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <p class="section-label">Two games every day</p>
    <h1 id="hero-heading">
      <span class="gradient-text">Two words. One rift.</span><br />
      Seven guesses and one decisive split.
    </h1>

    <p class="hero-sub">
      JopChi <span class="pronounce">(&ldquo;YOP-Chee&rdquo;)</span> is a
      twice-daily dual-word puzzle for iOS. Every game hides <strong>two five-letter words</strong> at once, and every guess is scored
      against both of them together. Morning Game 1 runs <strong>12:00 AM – 11:59 AM PT</strong>; Evening Game 2 runs <strong>12:00 PM – 11:59 PM PT</strong>.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-group" role="group" aria-label="Download options">
      <!-- App Store badge placeholder — replace href with real App Store URL before launch -->
      <a
        href="https://apps.apple.com"
        class="badge-cta app-store-badge"
        aria-label="Download JopChi on the App Store (link coming soon)"
        aria-describedby="app-store-note"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M18.71 19.5c-.83 1.24-1.71 2.45-3.05 2.47-1.34.03-1.77-.79-3.29-.79-1.53 0-2 .77-3.27.82-1.31.05-2.3-1.32-3.14-2.53C4.25 17 2.94 12.45 4.7 9.39c.87-1.52 2.43-2.48 4.12-2.51 1.28-.02 2.5.87 3.29.87.78 0 2.26-1.07 3.8-.91.65.03 2.47.26 3.64 1.98-.09.06-2.17 1.28-2.15 3.81.03 3.02 2.65 4.03 2.68 4.04-.03.07-.42 1.44-1.38 2.83M13 3.5c.73-.83 1.94-1.46 2.94-1.5.13 1.17-.34 2.35-1.04 3.19-.69.85-1.83 1.51-2.95 1.42-.15-1.15.41-2.35 1.05-3.11z"/>
        </svg>
        Download on the App Store
      </a>

      <!-- TestFlight beta link placeholder — replace href with real TestFlight invite URL before launch -->
      <a
        href="https://testflight.apple.com"
        class="badge-cta badge-cta-secondary"
        aria-label="Join the JopChi beta on TestFlight (link coming soon)"
        aria-describedby="testflight-note"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
          <path d="M12 2a10 10 0 1 1 0 20A10 10 0 0 1 12 2zm1 5h-2v6l5.25 3.15.75-1.23-4-2.42V7z"/>
        </svg>
        Join the Beta (TestFlight)
      </a>
    </div>

    <p id="app-store-note" class="badge-note" role="note">
      App Store link coming soon — currently in TestFlight beta.
    </p>
    <p id="testflight-note" class="badge-note" role="note">
      TestFlight invite link will be added before public launch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       How it works — The Rift mechanic
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="how-section" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
    <h2 id="how-heading">How the Rift Works</h2>

    <p class="how-intro">
      Two hidden words differ in <strong>exactly three letters</strong>. That
      difference is the <em>rift</em>. The other two letters are already shared,
      in the same correct positions &mdash; so every board begins with common
      ground and a gap to close.
    </p>

    <figure class="rift-demo">
      <figcaption class="rift-caption" aria-hidden="true">
        An example pair. Positions 1 and 5 are shared; positions 2, 3 and 4 are
        the rift.
      </figcaption>
      <!-- The tiles carry the shared/rift distinction in border style, which a
           screen reader cannot perceive, so the diagram is presentational and
           the equivalent information is given in prose below it. -->
      <div class="rift-rows" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="rift-row">
          <span class="rift-label">Word A</span>
          <span class="tile shared">C</span>
          <span class="tile differs">R</span>
          <span class="tile differs">A</span>
          <span class="tile differs">N</span>
          <span class="tile shared">E</span>
        </div>
        <div class="rift-row">
          <span class="rift-label">Word B</span>
          <span class="tile shared">C</span>
          <span class="tile differs">L</span>
          <span class="tile differs">O</span>
          <span class="tile differs">S</span>
          <span class="tile shared">E</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="rift-legend" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="key"><span class="swatch shared"></span> Shared letter</span>
        <span class="key"><span class="swatch differs"></span> Inside the rift</span>
      </p>
      <p class="sr-only">
        In this example Word A is CRANE and Word B is CLOSE. Both start with C
        and end with E, so those two letters are already shared and correctly
        placed. The middle three letters differ &mdash; R, A, N against L, O, S
        &mdash; and that is the rift you have to close.
      </p>
    </figure>

    <div class="rift-explanation card">
      <h3>Before the split</h3>
      <p>
        You guess a five-letter word and it is scored against both hidden words
        at once, on a single grid. A letter can be confirmed in one word, the
        other, or both &mdash; and when it is merely present rather than placed,
        the board deliberately will not tell you <em>which</em> word it belongs
        to. That ambiguity is the puzzle.
      </p>

      <h3>The split</h3>
      <p>
        After at least two guesses you may spend a turn on the <strong>Split</strong>: an irreversible move that breaks the board into
        two separate grids, one per word. From then on each guess is scored
        against each word independently. Split too early and you have little to
        go on; leave it too late and you run out of turns. Reach turn 6 without
        splitting and it fires automatically.
      </p>

      <h3>Winning</h3>
      <p>
        Eight turns, and the Split spends one of them &mdash; so seven guesses.
        You win by getting <strong>both</strong> words, and you must Split at
        some point to do it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============================================================
       Features
       ============================================================ -->
  <section class="features-section" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
    <h2 id="features-heading">Why JopChi?</h2>
    <ul class="features-grid" role="list">
      <li class="card feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">🌌</span>
        <h3>Daily challenge</h3>
        <p>Two fresh rifts every day at midnight and noon, the same pair for every player worldwide.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">♾️</span>
        <h3>Streak tracking</h3>
        <p>Build your streak, track your personal bests, and see daily stats on the leaderboard.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">♿</span>
        <h3>Accessible by design</h3>
        <p>Geometry mode carries every tile state in shape and position, so colour is never the only signal. Six validated palettes, plus a High Contrast mode. <a href="/accessibility">What is and is not built yet</a>.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="card feature-card">
        <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔒</span>
        <h3>Privacy first</h3>
        <p>No data brokers, no analytics resellers, and your stats are never sold. Play as a guest, or sign in only to sync your streak across devices.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 4rem 0 5rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero-glow {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 0%, rgba(109,40,217,0.35) 0%, transparent 70%);
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: -1;
  }

  .hero h1 { margin: 0.75rem 0 1.5rem; }

  .hero-sub {
    max-width: 42rem;
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .cta-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .app-store-badge {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a0533, var(--color-purple-mid));
    border: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
  }

  .badge-note {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .how-section { margin: 4rem 0; }

  .how-intro {
    max-width: 44rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .rift-demo {
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    /* Narrow screens scroll the diagram rather than the page */
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .rift-caption {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    max-width: 40rem;
  }

  .rift-rows {
    display: inline-grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .rift-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto repeat(5, 3rem);
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .rift-label {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    padding-right: 0.5rem;
    text-align: right;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Shape and border weight distinguish the two states, not hue alone —
     the same discipline Geometry mode uses in the app. */
  .tile {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
  }

  .tile.shared {
    border: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .tile.differs {
    border: 2px dashed var(--color-text-muted);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .rift-legend {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .rift-legend .key {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .swatch {
    width: 1rem;
    height: 1rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .swatch.shared { border: 2px solid var(--color-accent); }
  .swatch.differs { border: 2px dashed var(--color-text-muted); }

  .rift-explanation h3 {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .rift-explanation h3:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  /* Visually hidden, still announced */
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .pronounce {
    font-size: 0.9em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .rift-explanation p { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .rift-explanation p:first-child { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }

  .features-section { margin: 4rem 0 0; }

  .features-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .feature-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .feature-icon {
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
